{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/382250-vehicles-fuel-and-arcadia","id":382250,"title":"Vehicles, fuel and Arcadia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-26T13:52:28-08:00","id":382250,"title":"Vehicles, fuel and Arcadia","content":"A character I'm working on left her Keeper's realm by driving out in a van. The van was a part of the realm, but in mechanical terms it's a Token. It's a basic cargo-carrying panel van, nothing fancy. But I'm wondering what it ought to run on. I know that Tokens run on Glamour, but I'm thinking in terms of the Catch being to fill the gas tank with something unusual. If it helps, the van used to belong to a computer repair tech (don't ask). So perhaps iced tea or similar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T14:25:27-08:00","id":382318,"title":"","content":"Outside of their magic powers Tokens tend to work like any ordinary example of what they are. A token gun still fires bullets and a token sword is still sharp and pointy. As such I'd expect the van to still run on good old gasoline. But then technology, such as cars, often don't work in the hedge.<br /> <br /> Hedgespun is where you see the weird shit like cloths woven from moonlight or a gun that fires bees.<br /> <br /> What is the van's power? Whatever the Catch is, it'll allow for free use of the van's power and not act as a alternative fuel source, assuming standard Token behavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T14:33:53-08:00","id":382327,"title":"","content":"Nothing much. It's just a van. Maybe it reduces the base time for Hedge journeys, or permits rolls at shorter intervals. It's not hedgespun, though. It's purely Arcadian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T15:45:52-08:00","id":382397,"title":"","content":"It could always be a variant of Drivers Little Helper (CtL 203) in car form. Part of it's magic is the car running without needing gasoline so the van's magic is that it could run so long as the Catch in met.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T04:45:33-08:00","id":382933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/382250-vehicles-fuel-and-arcadia?p=382327#post382327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing much. It's just a van. Maybe it reduces the base time for Hedge journeys, or permits rolls at shorter intervals. It's not hedgespun, though. It's purely Arcadian.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aren't most tokens 'hedgespun' by definition? They look weird, but have a mask hiding their magical nature to non-changeling? The sole difference is that hedgespun tokens it is just the appearance, and they lack any game mechanical magical powers.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I have to agree with Helel, if you want the van to work without fuel use the Driver's Little Helper as a guideline, otherwise it functions as a normal vehicel in which case it would be simply hedgespun. Mind you, if you want it to actually work in the Hedge that in itself could be the magical part of the van. In the Hedge fuel such as glamor or weird somewhat rare goblin fruit would be the way to go. I certainly have trouble seeing a normal van driving through the Hedge: small narrow twisting paths flanked by dense bushes and very sharp long thorns make crappy roads for big lumbering vans <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T06:24:28-08:00","id":383007,"title":"","content":"Normal Tokens are mundane object that have been infused with Glamour while Hedgespun are made from hedge materials into magic items. Basically Tokens are the item version of changelings while Hedgespun are the item version of hobgoblins.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Artificer's Van (\u2022)</b></span><br /> This token appears to be nothing but a beat-up old van bearing the logo of a now defunct electronics store.The van hasHandling of -1, an Acceleration of 13, a Safe Speed of 60, and a maximum speed of 110. When activated the token can run without gasoline, even in the hedge (it cannot run in the hedge otherwise). Additionally while active the vehicle can safely drive over nearly any terrain that could be passed by an ATV.<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Mein:</b> When active the vehicle lets out an unearthly growl like rumble, the headlights take on the appearance of eyes, and the paint job of the van appears at a glance to be covered in orange fur.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> The token stays active as long as the engine is running. When it finally deactivates it breaks down with steam and smoke requiring 1 success per hour of driving to repair ( Wits + Crafts, 10 min per test).<br /> <b>Catch:</b> The Artificer's Van can be activated without glamour if the changeling feeds it with electronic devices, either a large number of defunct ones or one modern and working device, into the engine. These electronics are lost and will never be seen again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4692,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","user":"helel","date":". 01-27-2015, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T00:55:26-08:00","id":384048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>helel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/382250-vehicles-fuel-and-arcadia?p=383007#post383007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Normal Tokens are mundane object that have been infused with Glamour while Hedgespun are made from hedge materials into magic items. Basically Tokens are the item version of changelings while Hedgespun are the item version of hobgoblins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps true by the litteral sense of the world, but game mechanically speaking there is not much of a difference except in appearance between the two. If somebody wants their regular token be crafted in Arcadia and look really weird, but have the exact same powers as a 3-dot token I am not going to increase its cost because it has a mask and a weird appearance. In truth, the distinction feels a bit like Changeling hypocracy in trying to treat tokens as mundane items as opposed to the Fae stuff it is <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I like the van. Does it offer any benefit if used in the Hedge? How do you even travel at 60 miles per hour inside the Hedge? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Note btw that I think making it 1 dot is a bit cheap. How many resources does a PC need to have a normal van? Certainly more than 1. So I would go for 2 dots.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T09:30:46-08:00","id":384282,"title":"","content":"The effect is very much a one dot Token. The fact that it's a full sized van is, if anything, a drawback as it might prove difficult to take in some circumstances and you can't swap it out with a different car later. You're probably not going to pull 60 in the hedge but I did give it the ATV power so it can travel through the thorns albeit at the cost of scratching the thing up horribly. I imagine tho that the fur might help mitigate the damage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hedgespun fundimentaly works differently then Tokens, kinda. The rules for hedgespun creation in RoS point us towards good good equipment rather than activated magic. Gather enough ingredients and you can make some super strong armor or a dagger poisonous enough to kill almost anyone with a single strike. And then they introduce a bunch of example hedgespun not following their hedgespun creation rules AT ALL....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T11:51:29-08:00","id":384382,"title":"","content":"I do like that van. Thank you for that. The character I'm working on has many Tokens; her Durance basically consisted of playing through various laserdisc games from the inside. She earned her freedom by completing a marathon run through all of them, and was allowed to keep whatever she could take from one game/Realm to the next. From Thayer's Quest she took a belt pouch, about the size of a binoculars case, that can hold almost anthing, so long as the items can fit through the pouch's opening, and the Blood Sword of Iscar, which is simply a slightly curved sword that looks as though it had been roughly carved from crystal. In Dragon's Lair she gained a helm and a byrnie, and the fiery sword Dragonfang (along with some treasure from Singe's hoard). She took Ace' blaster from Space Ace, and Reika Kirishima's laser pistol from Time Gal, and drove back to Earth in Lance's van after she completed Braindead 13. The extra equipment helped a lot as she progressed through her freedom run. <br /> <br /> <br /> If you're wondering, yes, there were other games in her Durance, she just didn't take anything from them. In Cobra Command, for example, she piloted a helicopter gunship, but that wouldn't be helpful in other games or back on Earth. I chose Bloodbrute Ogre for kith and Seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 01-28-2015, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T19:59:30-08:00","id":384718,"title":"","content":"Fill it with hopes and dreams, make the exhaust pipe spew rainbows!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}